<title>BELGIUM: Recticel says outlook improving.</title>
<headline>Recticel says outlook improving.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian polyurethane foam maker Recticel SA said on Wednesday that the outlook for 1997 business was improving.</p>
<p>&quot;(In 1997) we expect a continuation of the already significant improvement in operating results seen in the second half of 1996,&quot; Recticel chief executive officer Luc Vansteenkiste told a news conference.</p>
<p>He said pre-tax operating profits in the second half of 1996 rose to 547 million francs, from 175 million in the first half.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
